                <pb facs="0236" n="214" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">399.10–UPU/1–2351:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Egypt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-01-24T15:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1951—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>707. For Caffery and Redding. Dept has taken fol
                    action re urtel 766. Mission Rio requested ask
                        FonOff instruct its delegate second and
                    speak in favor US motion. Mission Hague asked endeavor obtain Dutch affirmative
                    vote. In view Bern’s tel Jan 23 rptd Cairo Dept
                    doubts second approach Swiss wld be fruitful. Dept also doubts desirability second approach London or approach
                    Belgrade. Suggest Caffery continue endeavor obtain affirmative vote Egypt.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
